Hi Mairin,

That isn't an error but a warning. If the data are too coarse, then you can't estimate speed (see the Noonan et al. reference from the help file), but:
You may still be able to estimate diffusion rates (if you see them in the model-fit summary) and do meta-analysis on those.
Sometimes you can't estimate speed because the location-error model is insufficient. There is a vignette and cited pre-print covering this.
Why would this have given you problems with AKDE meta-analysis?

Best,
Chris

